emperature using PBS supplemented with 10 mM EDTA and subsequently washed with PBS. Cell pellets were frozen on dry ice and stored at −80°C. Frozen cell pellets were thawed on ice and suspended in 1 ml Lysis Buffer [IP Buffer (50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.4 at 4°C, 150 mM NaCl, 1 mM EDTA) supplemented with 0.5% Nonidet P 40 Substitute, protease and phosphatase inhibitor cocktails]. Affinity purifications were performed as follows. MagStrep “type3” beads (30 μl per sample) were equilibrated twice with Wash Buffer (IP Buffer supplemented with 0.05% NP40) and incubated with the lysate for 2 hours at 4°C. Following incubation, beads were washed twice with Wash Buffer and with IP Buffer. To directly digest bead-bound proteins, beads were resuspended in Denaturation-Reduction Buffer (2 M urea, 50 mM Tris-HCl pH 8.0, 1 mM DTT). Bead-bound proteins were denatured and reduced at 37°C for 30 minutes and after bringing them to room temperature, alkylated in the dark with 3 mM iodoacetamide for 45 minutes and quenched with 3 mM DTT for 10 minutes. Proteins were then digested with trypsin at 37°C. All steps were performed with constant shaking at 1,100 rpm. Peptides were desalted for MS analysis.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
